Superpermutation bounds in Lean: two upper bounds for large n (a Superpermutation Almanac batch)

This project contains Lean sources from two repositories, both under the Apache License 2.0, and new files.

Jay Pantone, superperm-upper-43-80
https://github.com/jaypantone/superperm-upper-43-80, commit c8fb7ffdd69be1375580710ae11b47a295b1f0f6
Apache License 2.0, reproduced in licenses/pantone-superperm-upper-43-80-LICENSE.
Included: Challenge.lean and the 94 modules of SuperpermutationUpperBound/ that the proofs import.
SuperpermutationUpperBound/Assembly/SupportedStates.lean is the modified copy of his file from
proofs/lean/constant/patches of github.com/jhalfar/superpermutations; it says at its top what was changed, and
patches/SupportedStates.diff shows the change. Six other files of his were changed for Lean 4.35.0 and the
Mathlib commit 56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679; each says at its top that it was changed and how.

Jakub Halfar, superpermutations
https://github.com/jhalfar/superpermutations, commit 64ab6a783731744882bc1886124faaf370fa9223,
directory proofs/lean/constant43586371
Apache License 2.0, reproduced in licenses/jhalfar-superpermutations-LICENSE.
Included: the 34 modules of SuperpermutationUpperBound43586371/ that the two statements need. Files changed for
Lean 4.35.0 say so at their top.

The six port fixes in files of the first repository and the one in Relabel.lean follow the compatibility
changes that Jay Pantone recorded for the same files in his release "A polynomial error estimate for
superpermutation length" (verification/compatibility.patch, Apache License 2.0).

SOURCES.tsv lists every included file with the SHA-256 of the original it was copied from.

New files: AlmanacSolution.lean, UpperLinks.lean, SuperpermutationUpperBound.lean,
SuperpermutationUpperBound43586371.lean, README.md. AlmanacDefs.lean, AlmanacStatement.lean and
AlmanacChallenge.lean are the Almanac's files (superpermutations.com), unchanged.
